    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>Wondrous Item, Rare (Requires Attunement)</em></p><p>Hundreds of pages of illustrations, tables, and diagrams about all sorts of monsters fill this magical tome.</p><p><strong>Charm Monster.</strong> While holding the book, you can cast @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplCharmMonst]{Charm Monster} (save DC 15) from it. A target that isn’t a Humanoid has Disadvantage on its saving throw against this spell. Once you cast the spell this way, you can’t do so again until the next dawn.</p><p><strong>Extensive Knowledge.</strong> When you attune to the book, you gain proficiency in one of the following skills of your choice: Arcana, History, Nature, or Religion. Whenever you finish a Long Rest, you can change your choice. If your Attunement to the book ends, you lose this proficiency.</p><p><strong>Monster Primer.</strong> While carrying the book, whenever you take the Study action to make an Intelligence (Arcana) check to recall information about an Aberration, a Construct, an Elemental, a Fey, or a Monstrosity you can see, a successful check also tells you whether that creature has any Immunities, Resistances, or Vulnerabilities, and if so, what they are.</p><section class=\"secret\" id=\"secret-G3zDiIJ9C9YdE1M0\"><p><strong>Foundry Note</strong></p><p>Activez dans l’onglet Effets l’effet <em>Extensive Knowledge</em> de la compétence choisie (un seul à la fois). Le Désavantage d’une cible non humanoïde contre <em>Charm Monster</em> est à appliquer à la main.</p></section>",
      "chat": ""
    },
